LINEAGE
The plugin is built against the kennel plugin SDK of Hundekraft 3.0.3 (https://github.com/Hundekraft/op1-workshop),
which is based on op1r-src by pcppcp (https://github.com/pcppcp/op1r-src); both are GPL-3.0-or-later with the same
additional permission (see their LICENSE and NOTICE files). The marker-jump logic ports op1r's tape/markers.c
jump semantics. No Teenage Engineering firmware, device key or NAND image is included or required to build.

REQUIRED CORE
Hundekraft 3.0.3 (kennel feature API OP1_FEATURE_API = 1). Built with the 3.0.3 source/SDK bundle
(SHA-256 of the bundle: 2f745e3858f9fabf8e653ecfe3511679b47f795ff09f13e9bd5590e26995b1d7).
Newer cores may work; older cores reject unknown imports at load time.

WHAT IT DOES (control map)
- Shift + Help (clock mode) -> T3 settings: the "MIDI MAP" switch row (green, white or red depending on
  registration order; it is the only switch registered today). Turn: mapping ON/OFF (setting op1midi.mmen).
- White encoder push in clock mode: opens the mapping editor (modal overlay, 320x160).
- Editor: blue = MIDI channel (1..16 / ALL), green = CC/PC number (push toggles CC <-> PC), white = action
  (turn; push = value edit for TAPE/INSTRUMENT, push again = validate), red = row cursor over 16 rows
  (4 pages, the cursor row is drawn red, others white), left/right = pages, Shift + Help = validate and close
  (settings op1midi.mmr0..mmr15, one packed int32 per row).
- Actions: MARKER NEXT / MARKER PREV (jump via the core's shared markers tm_pos[]/tm_n and
  op1_tape_pos_set), PLAY FROM MARKER (locate + op1_seq_press_play; only from stop, no punch, no armed
  count-in), TAPE SELECT (value 1..4 -> op1_tape_switch), INSTRUMENT SELECT (no core service yet: a toast
  explains it once per boot).
- Mapped CCs are taken from the core's key/encoder path (op1_midi_take_cc). Default mapping (empty user
  config): CC 80 next, CC 81 previous, CC 82 play-from-marker, channel 1.

CLAIMS
- key:clock:white (the white encoder push in clock mode; no other plugin consumes it in 3.0.3).

BUILD
- hundekraft-plugin/build-knl.sh <path to the 3.0.3 source bundle> — packs synth_sdk/plugins/op1midi
  with the bundle's tools/kennel/pack.py inside the bfin-elf Docker toolchain. Output: op1midi.knl.

INSTALL
- Workshop (https://hundekraft.github.io/op1-workshop/): Your plugins -> add op1midi.knl -> Update OP-1 ->
  confirm with T1 on the OP-1 prompt. Takes effect at the confirmed restart. Removal and conflicts are
  managed by the workshop. Save a disk-mode backup first (see install-recuperation.md in the repository).

CHANGES
- v3.1 (2026-10-28): MARKER destination is now flat 1..32 — in core 3.0.3 the marker set is
  SHARED across the four tapes, so the number is the n-th placed marker on the current tape and
  no tape switch happens (use the TAPE destination to change tapes; MRK+/MRK- still navigate).
  SOUND 1..8 is now functional without a core service: Shift + blue press in the editor arms a
  learn whose capture depends on the row's destination — for SOUND the next sound-key press
  (T1..T4, Shift+T1..T4 for slots 5..8) is captured (the key is swallowed, nothing moves);
  playback injects synthetic keys into the stock key queue (R246 addresses 0x01DD5044 /
  0x01DD5244 / 0x01DD5248 / 0x01DD524D, wake 0x019C2F04 — the same mechanism the firmware's
  MIDI-key path uses): SYNTH press/release, then Shift + T_n for slots 5..8. MIDI learn still
  captures NOTE/CC/PC for every other destination. 17 imports, all present in kn_exports.c.
- v3 (2026-10-28): new mapping model per the user's v3 spec (midi-spec.md, gui-layout.md).
  Sources: NOTE (note-on vel > 0; mapped notes are swallowed in the note pipeline, MIDI source
  only), CC (rising edge >= 64), PC (every message). Destinations: SOUND 1..8 (no core service
  yet: a toast explains it once per boot), TAPE 1..4 (op1_tape_switch; the core stops playback
  itself; recording/disk errors ignored), MUTE 1..4 (toggle of the R246 mute byte 0xFF8010A0+t
  plus the DSP refresh call 0x01967ED0 — stock addresses, not exported services), MARKER global
  1..124 (tape = (g-1)/31+1, local = (g-1)%31+1; note: in core 3.0.3 the marker set is SHARED
  across the four tapes — the switch + local index still resolve, semantics to validate),
  MRK+ / MRK- (kept from v2). Global MIDI channel back in the UI: Shift + green turn in the
  editor cycles OFF/1..16/ALL (setting mmch). Fade (Shift + white turn in the editor, setting
  mmfade: OFF/1s/2s/8s/32s): while playing, every marker jump fades the four tape track volumes
  (live words 0xFF801928 + ranges 0xFF8018CC, R246) to zero, jumps at silence (tape switch and
  locate run on the main loop; a cross-tape jump locates at OP1_EV_TAPE_SWITCH after), fades back
  and restores exactly; STOP during a fade cancels the jump and restores. MIDI learn: Shift +
  blue press in the editor arms it (LRN shown), the next NOTE/CC/PC writes the source of the
  cursor row (default destination TAPE on an empty row; the learned CC is taken at once).
  Editor v3: live editing (no validation mode), columns in the encoder colours, cursor row red,
  header MIDI MAP pX/4 CH:x F:x (LRN while learning). Settings format versioned by 'mmv' = 3
  (older rows reset). 17 imports, all present in kn_exports.c.
- v2 (2026-10-28): hardware-test fixes. Settings row registered at OP1_EV_BOOT_DONE (after the
  built-ins) so MIDI SEQ keeps the green row and MIDI MAP takes the white one; the editor overlay
  now draws a full-screen fade plus an opaque black panel with a white border before its text
  (pattern of the kennel's randomiser plugin); new exits from the modal editor, all saving:
  Help (Shift or not), the mode keys (help, metronome, synth, drum, tape, mixer, sequencer, mic,
  COM), T1..T4 and transport REC/PLAY/STOP — without Shift the key then acts as usual, with Shift
  it is consumed.
- v1 (2026-10-27): first release. 16-row CC/PC mapping editor, marker jumps, play from marker,
  tape select, settings switch, modal overlay editor. Compiled with bfin-elf-gcc 13.3.0.

